cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or adapt the Agent Emergency Protocol, please cite it as below and credit \"Agent Emergency Protocol (AEP), created by Mitthan Meena\"."
title: "Agent Emergency Protocol (AEP) v0.1 — Draft Specification"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Meena
    given-names: Mitthan
version: "0.1-draft"
date-released: "2026-10-06"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/mitthanmeena-ops/agent-emergency-protocol"
abstract: >-
  Agent Emergency Protocol: a vendor-neutral runtime emergency-code language
  for autonomous AI agents.
  Each incident gets a short code, a severity level (L1 Watch to L5 Ground),
  a default first response and a standard, hash-chained evidence record,
  with mappings to MITRE ATLAS, MITRE ATT&CK and NIST SP 800-53 evidence.
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - agent security
  - incident response
  - emergency codes
  - MITRE ATLAS
  - NIST SP 800-53
